 For $x > 8,$
\begin{align*}
\frac{x^2}{x - 8} &= \frac{x^2 - 64 + 64}{x - 8} \\
&= \frac{(x + 8)(x - 8) - 64}{x - 8} \\
&= x + 8 - \frac{64}{x - 8}
\end{align*}By AM-GM, $\frac{64}{x - 8} \le 8,$ so
\[x + \frac{64}{x - 8} \ge x - 8 + 8 = x.\]Therefore,
\[x + 8 - \frac{64}{x - 8} \ge x + 8 - 8 = x.\]As $x$ approaches 8 from the right, we get that our minimum value is $\boxed{8}.$

The differentiation problem can also be solved by noting that
\[\frac{d}{dx} \left( x + 8 - \frac{64}{x - 8} \right) = 1 + \frac{64}{(x - 8)^2}.\]Thus, the function $f(x) = \frac{x^2}{x - 8}$ has no critical points, and as $x$ increases, this function also increases.

